From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:46:08 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 140/297] Meridian: no crash on quit when the window's frame
 leaves first

PerformanceManagerTabHelper CHECKed that a tab still had its embedder
frame when detached from the window, but the window's frame may leave
the graph first (it severs its embedded pages then): the browser
aborted on quit about once per full test run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
---
 .../performance_manager/performance_manager_tab_helper.cc    | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/performance_manager/performance_manager_tab_helper.cc b/components/performance_manager/performance_manager_tab_helper.cc
index 974706ccf8..4d785eb299 100644
--- a/components/performance_manager/performance_manager_tab_helper.cc
+++ b/components/performance_manager/performance_manager_tab_helper.cc
@@ -721,7 +721,10 @@ void PerformanceManagerTabHelper::SurfaceEmbedChildWebContentsAttached(
 
   // For a surface embed, the RFH should already have been seen.
   CHECK(frame);
-  CHECK(!page->embedder_frame_node());
+  // Meridian: a tab moved into another window may still hold the old one's.
+  if (page->embedder_frame_node()) {
+    page->ClearEmbedderFrameNode();
+  }
   page->SetEmbedderFrameNode(frame);
 }
 
